  "data_scale": "scale 1: 100k frames over 60 days of working hours on 2 monitors (sessions of 40 frames; 30 apps, Chrome/Slack/VS Code hold ~35 %; 8 % of frames lost their app name), OCR/accessibility full_text on 95 % (~134 chars, frames_fts), 72k accessibility elements (elements_fts), 50k ui_events (ui_events_fts), 1k video chunks backing the oldest 60 % of frames, 24k audio chunks with 41k transcriptions (audio_transcriptions_fts), 40 speakers, 6.9k diarization segments, 80 meetings with 4.8k live transcript segments; 161 MB, builds in ~2 s. Scale 4: 400k frames in the same 60 days, 650 MB, ~9 s",
  "visibility_note": "22k stars; desktop app for macOS/Windows/Linux that records the screen and audio 24/7 into a local SQLite database, which reporters describe at 50-77 GB",
  "interest_note": "Activity summary: two MATERIALIZED CTEs resolve every frame's app through correlated ui_events fallbacks, then a dozen CTEs of GROUP BY, ROW_NUMBER and LEAD() gap windows over JULIANDAY under a 4-way UNION ALL; key texts CROSS JOIN elements with ROW_NUMBER over LENGTH/CASE; FTS5 external-content search with column filters, bm25 LIMIT 5000 IN-subqueries and tag GROUP BY/HAVING; retention NOT IN anti-joins and trigger-heavy deletes.",
  "reach": 1,
